<title>AUSTRIA: SAUDI SAYS OPEC HAS 100 PCT COMMITMENT TO QUOTAS.</title>
<headline>SAUDI SAYS OPEC HAS 100 PCT COMMITMENT TO QUOTAS.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabian oil minister Ali bin Ibrahim al-Naimi said on Wednesday that OPEC had a high level of commitment towards keeping output allocations.</p>
<p>&quot;We have a very high level of commitment...one hundred percent,&quot; he told reporters.  </p>
<p>Earlier, OPEC agreed to freeze its 25.033 million barrels per day (bpd) output ceiling until the end of the year, while members said they would adhere to their individual quotas.</p>
<p>The oil price jumped on the news with North Sea Brent Blend ending 35 cents higher on the London futures market at $18.21 a barrel.</p>
<p>Prices had fallen from around $25 in January with overproduction by some OPEC members cited as one of the reasons for the decline. OPEC's overall production has been running at around 2.0 million bpd above the group's ceiling.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
